Allow a static libstdc++ on webOS.

Firefox refuses to link libstdc++ statically because official builds must use
the distribution's copy. On webOS the TV's libstdc++ varies by firmware (GCC 6
on webOS 4, GCC 11 on webOS 25), so this build links it statically and hides
its symbols with --exclude-libs (build/mozconfig-arm32, build/mozconfig-nc4);
the TV's Mali driver keeps using the TV's own copy. Warn instead of failing.

diff --git a/build/moz.configure/flags.configure b/build/moz.configure/flags.configure
index 4822831ac5..ca83795b4f 100644
--- a/build/moz.configure/flags.configure
+++ b/build/moz.configure/flags.configure
@@ -76,7 +76,10 @@ def link_libstdcxx_statically(
 
 @depends(when=link_libstdcxx_statically)
 def check_libstdcxx_linkage():
-    die("Firefox does not support linking statically with libstdc++")
+    log.warning(
+        "Linking libstdc++ statically: its symbols must be hidden "
+        "(--exclude-libs) because the TV's GPU driver loads the shared one"
+    )
 
 
 check_and_add_flag(
